  "explanation": "The question asks when the 'Cross of Liberty' was established. Two distinct referents appear in the sources: one related to Estonia and another to Finland. For the Estonian Cross of Liberty, two documents (D1S1 and D2S1) state it was established on 24 February 1919, while two others (D3S1 and D4S1) claim 12 March 1920. These are distinct valid answers for the same award, likely reflecting updates or re-establishments. The Finnish 'Order of the Cross of Liberty' (D5S3) was founded on March 4, 1918, but this refers to a different entity and scope, so it is excluded from the final answer list."
